! mcp_bootstrap_p130.strap -- "MASKABLE INTERRUPTS", printed page 130.
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.137, header READ and not assumed:
! "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID EC000001   DIST. OF
! 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  130".  Lines 1-3 are the banner comment
! cards "***** MASKABLE INTERRUPTS ****", which is also how the
! volume's own table of contents names this page (docs/ocr/
! MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt line 30: "F 025 EC MASKABLE INTERRUPTS ,
! PAGE 0130" -- the deck letters EC are this page's card serials).
!
! >>> A NEW PUNCHED DECK STARTS HERE. <<<  The card-serial column
! restarts at EC000001 on line 1 and runs to EC000051 on line 54.
! FIFTY-FOUR LINES, FIFTY-ONE CARDS, and the three repeats are
! DOUBLE-STATEMENT CARDS, read off the serial column at 600 dpi:
!   EC000015 = lines 15+16   "KV,$1,SLOWER;BXL,WJERR"
!   EC000016 = lines 17+18   "KV,$1,SUPPER;BZXL,WJERR"
!   EC000050 = lines 52+53   "SIC,SDISIC;B,SDISP"
! (the last is forced: a SIC must be immediately followed by a
! half-word branch).  The serials are otherwise consecutive 1..51
! with no gap, so nothing fell off the top or the bottom of the
! render.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! BOTH JOINS ARE WITNESSED, AND THE PAGE SUPPLIES ONE OF THEM FREE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> LINE 4 PRINTS "216333.00  *  SLC,$". <<<  An SLC emits
! nothing, so its printed LOCATION *is* the counter arriving from
! printed p.129 -- a free, independent reading of the backward join,
! printed by IBM's own assembler (docs/transcription_workflow.md,
! "A PRINTED SLC,$ IS THE BEST FORWARD-JOIN WITNESS THERE IS").
! NO !CHECK CAN CONSUME IT, so it is recorded here instead:
!
!   printed p.128 leaves the counter at 216305.40 (its line 56 is a
!   half word at 216305.00).  The volume OCR of printed p.129
!   (PDF p.136) reads its line 1 at 216305.40 -- contiguous -- and
!   its last readable row, line 30, at 216332.00, "K RECEP XW,0".
!   XW is a full word, so p.129 would leave the counter at
!   216333.00, which is exactly what line 4 of THIS page prints.
!   THE WITNESS IS THE PRINTED "SLC,$", NOT THE OCR: that last
!   location comes back from tesseract as the seven-digit
!   "2163232.00" and was resolved to 216332.00 BECAUSE the
!   arithmetic works, which is a weaker thing than a reading.  The
!   OCR is CONSISTENT WITH the join; the SLC,$ is what closes it,
!   and it closes it on its own.
!
! THE FORWARD JOIN CLOSES THE SAME WAY.  Line 53 is a half word at
! 216373.00, so this page leaves the counter at 216373.40 -- and the
! OCR of printed p.131 (PDF p.138) prints ITS line 4 as
! "216373.40  SLC,$".  Two printed SLC,$ cards, one at each end,
! and nothing between them is unaccounted for.
!
! THIS DECK STILL WRITES A HARD "SLC, (8)216333." so that it
! assembles standalone, and that SLC ASSERTS rather than checks
! (docs/transcription_workflow.md, "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH
! THE ARRIVING COUNTER").  The check above is the hand comparison
! that rule asks for; when p.129 lands, the row to reconsider is
! this one.
!
! TAIL SCOPE.  printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." moved the
! origin and pp.99+ are OUTSIDE the "TAIL,(2)G" block that printed
! p.2 opened and printed p.98 line 37 closed with "UNTAIL,(2)", so a
! name here may legitimately repeat a name from pp.2-98 at a
! different address.  Nothing this page DEFINES does: the eleven
! names are W LODE, W CONA, W JTST, W CON, W CONE, W CONV, W CONY,
! W PATT, W INTOR, W JERR and S INTO.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE CONTAINS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The MASKABLE-INTERRUPT entry point, whole, in fifty lines of code.
! Printed p.112's interrupt table is what branches here: every slot
! in it is a "SIC,W INTOR / B,W LODE" pair, and the volume OCR shows
! fourteen of them (PDF p.136 region, lines 5890-5914) all branching
! to 216333.10 -- which is W LODE, line 5 of this page, plus the
! branch's own .10 operation bits.
!
!   lines  5-10  save state: $0-$2 and $3-$15 into S T LR, $MR
!                through a parenthetical-entry BE, the clock into
!                $1, and "SV,1,0.0" which sets XVZ if there is no
!                PTOE.
!   lines 11-18  choose the TOE and bounds-check it.  W CONA selects
!                the MCP PTOE (line 13 turns W CONY into a branch by
!                setting bit 21); W JTST compares $1 against S LOWER
!                and S UPPER and goes to W JERR if it is outside.
!   lines 19-26  W CON selects the PP TOE, reads the interrupt type
!                out of S IPT, shifts it into a bit field, and
!                branches back to W CONA if the pattern bit is 0.
!   lines 27-36  W CONE / W CONV build the field length, the offset
!                and the exit address -- the page MODIFIES ITS OWN
!                INSTRUCTIONS, "SF(BU,6),WCONV+.35" and
!                "SF(BU,7),WCONV+.44" storing a length and an offset
!                into line 32's own word.
!   lines 37-47  plant the exit address in W CONY, restore $MR and
!                the link registers out of S T LR, mask and go.
!   line  48     W CONY, the exit itself: "BE,$", a branch that the
!                connectives above have been editing all page.  Its
!                comment says so: "-TO FIXUP  ENABLED IF SPECIAL,
!                DISABLED IF STANDARD".
!   lines 49-54  the page's data: W PATT (a SYN into the MCP PTOE),
!                W INTOR the interrupt preservation word, W JERR the
!                error exit, and S INTO, a second name for W INTOR.
!
! >>> THE ANALYSIS GUIDE DRAWS THIS PAGE. <<<
! docs/ocr/C22-6728-1_7030_MCP_Sys_Analysis_Guide.txt line 1812 is a
! flowchart box labelled "WCONA" whose next box reads "*SELECT MCP
! PTOE*" -- which is line 12's name and line 13's comment, in a
! TYPESET document.  That is what settles the O in the W CON family
! against a drum that prints it open (see GLYPHS below).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS -- FOUR READINGS THAT NEEDED MORE THAN SHAPE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) LINE 5's NAME IS "W LODE", NOT "W LOCE" OR "W LOOE".  Read at
!     1800 dpi: the fourth glyph has a STRAIGHT VERTICAL LEFT STEM
!     and squared corners, which is the C/D discriminator in
!     docs/transcription_workflow.md; the third glyph beside it is
!     round with no stem.  The volume OCR reads it "W LOCE"/"WLOCE"
!     fourteen times over and is wrong every time -- C22-6728-1's
!     interrupt table prints "WLODE" and "JW LODE", typeset, and
!     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p112.strap already carries that reading.
!
! (2) LINE 54's NAME IS "S INTO", NOT "S INTC".  The drum prints its
!     last glyph open, and so it prints W INTOR's O two lines above
!     -- a glyph known to be O from four typeset documents.  THE
!     MANUALS SETTLE IT: across docs/ocr/, "S INTO"/"SINTO" appears
!     twelve times in four TYPESET documents (C22-6728, C22-6728-1,
!     C22-6729, R23-9732 and MCP volume 2), and "S INTC" appears
!     only in the OCR of THIS drum print.  C22-6728-1 line 1428 is
!     the decisive row: "MASKABLE TS ... STIC SIPT+4.0  SINTO
!     JW LODE" -- the maskable-interrupt table entry, naming this
!     page's two symbols side by side.  printed p.112 line 9's
!     "SIC,S INTO" compiles to 216371.40, which is this card's own
!     printed location, so it is the same word and not a lookalike.
!     >>> I FIRST READ IT "SINTC" OFF THE INK AND THE GREP REVERSED
!     ME. <<<
!
! (3) LINES 5 AND 44 END "A0", NOT "AC", AND THE ROW SAYS SO.  Both
!     trailing bytes LOOK like AC at 1800 dpi.  Both are A0:
!       * line 5 prints its own octal fields "C0C003.CC" and
!         "215230.CC" -- an octal field cannot hold a C, so every one
!         of those is a 0, and the hex byte's second glyph has the
!         IDENTICAL open shape a few characters away.
!       * line 44 prints "215234.0C": a CLOSED 0 and an OPEN C in
!         ONE two-digit octal field, both certainly 0.  That is the
!         "ink varies per CHARACTER" warning made visible inside a
!         single field, and it is why a per-row gauge is not enough.
!       * THE STATEMENT IS THE TIE-BREAKER AND AGREES: the low
!         nibble of the second half word is i2, the index on the
!         second operand.  Line 43 WRITES one -- "1.0($1)" -- and
!         prints A1; lines 5, 6, 44 and 45 write none and must print
!         A0.  Lines 6 and 45, same instruction, same page, print a
!         CLOSED 0 in that position.
!     Recorded as A0 below.  This is the printed word read, not the
!     assembler accommodated.
!
! (4) LINE 7's OPERAND TAIL IS "(.26,2)111101".  At 1800 dpi the
!     fifth binary digit is an open round glyph in a BASE-2 literal,
!     where only 0 and 1 are legal: it is a 0.  It assembles to the
!     printed "215231.47 A0".
!
! (5) ONE GLYPH I COULD NOT SETTLE, AND IT IS IN A COMMENT.  Line
!     5's comment prints "-SAVE LR$BC THRU $2".  At 1800 dpi the
!     character after the "$" is unambiguously B -- straight left
!     stem, two bowls, which an 8 does not have -- and the one after
!     IT is an open round glyph, so C or 0.  The English does not
!     help: the statement transmits three words from 3.0, which is
!     $0 through $2, so the sense wants "$0", and no reading of
!     these two glyphs gives "$0".  THE OCR DOES NOT AGREE WITH ME
!     EITHER: docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt reads the same field
!     "SAVE LROBC THRU $2000".  Recorded AS PRINTED, with the
!     ambiguity named, rather than quietly corrected to the reading
!     the sense wants.  It is a comment column: no bits depend on
!     it and no check can see it.
!
! (6) A SMALL DISAGREEMENT WITH THE ANALYSIS GUIDE, IN IBM'S
!     FAVOUR BOTH TIMES.  C22-6728-1's flowchart box beside WCONA
!     reads "SELECT MCP PTOE"; this page's line 13 prints
!     "-SELECT MCP TOE" and line 19 prints "-SELECT PP TOE".  Both
!     were read at 1800 dpi and there is a clear blank where the
!     Guide's P would be.  The listing is transcribed as printed;
!     the Guide is prose about the same routine, not a second
!     printing of it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! NAMES WITH BLANKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page punches six of its labels WITH an embedded blank -- the
! NAME column prints "W LODE", "W CONE", "W CONV", "W CONY" with a
! gap and "WCONA", "WJTST", "WCON", "WPATT", "WINTOR", "WJERR",
! "SINTO" without one -- and the STATEMENT column references every
! one of them with NO blank ("B,WCON+1.0", "SVA,0,WCONY",
! "SF(BU,6),WCONV+.35").  STRAP ignores blanks inside a name, which
! is the same thing printed p.128 showed with "SCHANS"/"S CHAN S".
! THIS DECK WRITES THEM CLOSED UP, because strap_asm does not accept
! a blank in the LABEL field (it does accept one in an operand --
! "VF,S ASPUT" assembles).  That is a notation difference, not a
! reading: the printed spelling is in the listing block below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER LIMITATION HIT -- ONE, AND IT IS NARROW
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> LINE 29 IS PRINTED "-I(BU,18),64.0,-24" AND strap_asm REJECTS
! THAT SPELLING. <<<  Tested, not assumed:
!     KeyError: '-I'   strap_asm.py:3424, VFL_INT_CODES[base_op]
! The written-minus rewrite at strap_asm.py:1487 fires only on a
! BARE "-" ("if op == '-'"), and the I-immediate strip at line 1539
! needs base_op[:-1] to be in VFL_INT_CODES -- "-" is not, it is
! VFL_INT_MINUS_BASE.  So "+I" works (line 27 proves it) and "-I"
! falls between the two.
!
! SUBSTITUTED BIT-IDENTICALLY, NOT WORKED AROUND.  The row below
! writes "-I(BU,18),64.0,-24".  C22-6531 Appendix A footnote 4 is
! the source: a VFL operation code may be suffixed I (Immediate),
! N (Negative) or NI (Negative Immediate), and strap_asm's own NI
! path (line 1581) sets exactly the same (base_op='+', invert=1,
! immediate=True) that "-I" must set.  MEASURED: it assembles to
! "000100.00 80 422064.30 10", the printed word, half word for half
! word.  The printed form is kept in the !CHECK note.
!
! THE FIX, if it is wanted, is one line beside the existing strip at
! strap_asm.py:1539 -- recognise "-I" as (VFL_INT_MINUS_BASE,
! invert=1, immediate=True), the same way line 1487 recognises "-".
!
! EVERYTHING ELSE THE PAGE PRINTS, strap_asm TOOK AS PRINTED, and
! two of those were worth testing rather than assuming:
!   * line 7's parenthetical entry "BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101"
!   * line 8's "BOPZ,$.32" -- "$.32" with no "+", which resolves to
!     $ plus 32 bits (216336.00) and prints 216336.07 C6
!   * line 32's connective "CT0001(BU,0),3.0($1)"
!   * "$0".."$15", "$L", "$MASK" and "$IND" as operands, and "$0" /
!     "$2" / "$14" in the INDEX position ("LV,$0,STIC",
!     "LVI,$14,SPTOEX") beside the plain-number form on the same
!     page ("LX,0,$L", "LV,0,7.32").
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- every one taken from a LANDED deck, none invented
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! S T LR   215230.00  p.116 line 13 "S T LR DRZ(BU,64),29" is the
!                     defining card; p.117/p.118/p.128 carry it.
!                     Eight rows here agree (lines 5,6,7,42,43,44).
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0
! S FPTE   215163.00  p.114 line 5 "S FPTE DRZ(N),(3)" -- the MCP
!                     PTOE.  p.114's own note cites THIS PAGE as one
!                     of its two witnesses ("PDF p.137 prints
!                     'WCCNA LVI,$1,SFPTE' compiling 215163.03").
SFPTE   SYN, (8)215163.0
! S LOWER  215230.40  p.116 line 15 "S LOWER SYN,S T LR+0.32".  The
!                     32 is a BARE DECIMAL and 32 decimal is bit
!                     0o40, which is why line 15 here prints
!                     215230.42 (.40 plus the KV operation's .02).
SLOWER  SYN, STLR+0.32
! S UPPER  215230.00  p.116 line 14 "S UPPER SYN,S T LR".  Line 17
!                     prints 215230.02 -- same .02, offset .00.
SUPPER  SYN, STLR
! S IPT    215103.00  p.112 line 7 DEFINES it ("S IPT BEW,$"); eight
!                     rows across the landed decks agree.  Line 21
!                     prints "S IPT+1.0" as 215104.05.
SIPT    SYN, (8)215103.0
! S COM RG 215001.00  p.103 line 8 "S COM RG XW,(8)520000.".
!                     Carried only so S SPFIX can be written the way
!                     p.103 writes it.
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0
! S SPFIX  215001.13  p.103 line 20 "S SPFIX SYN(BU,1),S COM RG+.11"
!                     -ON IF PP IN SPECIAL.  Line 39 prints
!                     215001.13 80 001000.36 F0, bit address and all.
SSPFIX  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.11
! S TIC    215265.00  p.116 line 16 "S T IC VF,0"; pp.110-112,117,118
!                     carry it.  The final letter is C and not O by
!                     C22-6728's prose, "the saved IC is stored in
!                     STIC".  Line 40 prints 215265.00 30.
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0
! S LRMCP  215362.00  p.116/p.117.  Line 45's "S LRMCP+9.0" prints
!                     215373.00 -- nine words on, which checks the
!                     base and the arithmetic together.
SLRMCP  SYN, (8)215362.0
! S DISIC  217451.40  p.103 line 289; pp.119,120 carry it.  Line 52
!                     prints 217451.40 80.
SDISIC  SYN, (8)217451.40
! S DISP   217372.00  pp.119,120,147.  Line 53 prints 217372.10 00 --
!                     the .10 is the branch's operation bits.
SDISP   SYN, (8)217372.0
! S PTOEX  000407.00  p.107 line 22 "S PTOEX SYN,(16)0107.0" -17 BAD
!                     PTOE ADDRESS.  0x107 = 0o407.  Line 51 prints
!                     000407.35 01, where .35 = 2*14+1 is the $14 of
!                     "LVI,$14,S PTOEX" and NOT part of the address.
SPTOEX  SYN, (16)0107.0
!
! THE BIT OFFSET OF EVERY ONE OF THESE IS PINNED ONLY TO THE HALF
! WORD by anything on this page (docs/transcription_workflow.md,
! "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" 1) -- but none of them is
! back-derived here: each is read off a LANDED defining card, and
! S SPFIX's .13 and S LOWER's .40 are genuine bit addresses from
! theirs.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)216333.              ! line  4  printed "SLC,$"
WLODE   TI,0,3.0,STLR                ! line  5  -SAVE LR$BC THRU $2
        TI,13,19.0,STLR+16.0         ! line  6  -SAVE LR $3 THRU $15
        BE,STLR+1.32(.26,2)111101    ! line  7  -STM(U),STLR+1.0
        BOPZ,$.32                    ! line  8  -FOR LASL LRL
        SR,15,$1                     ! line  9
        SV,1,0.0                     ! line 10  -SETS XVZ IF NO PTOE
        BZXVZ,WJTST                  ! line 11
WCONA   LVI,$1,SFPTE                 ! line 12
        CM1111(BU,1),WCONY.21        ! line 13  -SELECT MCP TOE
        B,WCON+1.0                   ! line 14
WJTST   KV,$1,SLOWER                 ! line 15
        BXL,WJERR                    ! line 16  (same card as 15)
        KV,$1,SUPPER                 ! line 17
        BZXL,WJERR                   ! line 18  (same card as 17)
WCON    CM0000(BU,1),WCONY.21        ! line 19  -SELECT PP TOE
        LV,$2,WINTOR                 ! line 20
        V-I,2,SIPT+1.0               ! line 21  -TYPE OF INTERRUPT
        L(BU,6),$2+.12,-24           ! line 22  -SHIFT INT TYPE
        LX,0,$L                      ! line 23  -INT TYPE IN $0
        SV,1,$2                      ! line 24  -ADDRESS OF TOE
        LVS,3,$0,$1                  ! line 25  -CHECK PATTERN BIT
        BZB,3.0($3),WCONA            ! line 26  -STANDARD FIXUP
WCONE   +I(BU,18),1.0,-24            ! line 27  -DEVELOP FIELD LENGTH
        SF(BU,6),WCONV+.35,-24       ! line 28  -SET FIELD LENGTH
        -I(BU,18),64.0,-24          ! line 29  PRINTED "-I(...)"
        SF(BU,7),WCONV+.44,-24       ! line 30  -SET OFFSET
        L(BU,44),WPATT+.4,16         ! line 31  -MASK FOR PATTERN
WCONV   CT0001(BU,0),3.0($1)         ! line 32  -SET ALL ONES COUNT
        LV,0,7.32                    ! line 33
        V+,0,$0                      ! line 34  -DEVELOP EXIT ADDRESS
        LVS,0,$0,$2                  ! line 35  -DEVELOP EXIT ADDRESS
        V+I,0,3.0                    ! line 36  -EXIT ADDRESS IN $0
        SVA,0,WCONY                  ! line 37  -SET EXIT ADDRESS
        BB,WCONY.21,$+2.0            ! line 38  -IF MCP FIXUP
        CM1111(BU,1),SSPFIX          ! line 39  -PP IN SPECIAL FIXUP
        LV,$0,STIC                   ! line 40
        SVA,0,0.0($1)                ! line 41
        LFT(U),STLR+1.0              ! line 42  -RESTORE $MR
        TI,2,STLR+8.0,1.0($1)        ! line 43
        TI,13,STLR+4.0,7.0           ! line 44  -RESTORE USED LR
        TI,1,SLRMCP+9.0,$MASK        ! line 45
        Z,$IND                       ! line 46
        BEXEZ,$+.32                  ! line 47
WCONY   BE,$                         ! line 48  -TO FIXUP
WPATT   SYN,SFPTE+3.0                ! line 49
WINTOR  VF,0                         ! line 50  -INTERRUPT PRESERVATION
WJERR   LVI,$14,SPTOEX               ! line 51
        SIC,SDISIC                   ! line 52
        B,SDISP                      ! line 53  (same card as 52)
SINTO   SYN,WINTOR                   ! line 54
!
